---
import Marketing from "../layouts/Marketing.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";

const commitments = [
  "Every number on every screen can show its raw evidence. If we can't show the receipt, we don't show the number.",
  "Uncertainty is labeled, not smoothed. \"Unexplained\" stays on the chart, striped, with its real share.",
  "Your query sets and results are never used to train anything, and never shown to anyone else.",
  "When our method changes, your history is recomputed and the change is flagged on your chart — not corrected quietly."
];
---

<Marketing
  title="About"
  description="Why Citerate exists, what we commit to, and who is accountable for the number. A measurement product is only worth the trust you place in the people making the measurement."
>
  <section class="section section--flush" style="padding-top:72px;padding-bottom:72px">
    <div class="wrap wrap--prose">
      <div class="stack stack--4">
        <span class="t-label">About</span>
        <h1 class="t-d1">We built the instrument we wanted to be handed.</h1>
        <p style="font:400 19px/1.65 var(--font-display);color:var(--ink-soft);margin:0">
          A measurement product is only worth the trust you place in the people making the measurement. So
          here's who we are and what we've committed to.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:28px">
        <p>
          In 2025, the reports stopped making sense. Impressions held, positions held, clicks fell. Every tool
          on the market drew the same falling line and none of them could say why — because the cause wasn't in
          the data any of them collected. The answer above the links had started citing three sources, and you
          were either one of them or you weren't.
        </p>
        <p>
          Citerate exists to measure that one thing carefully, and to say plainly when it can't. It is
          deliberately not an AI content generator, not a rank tracker with a new label, and not a dashboard
          that reframes uncertainty as insight.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="stack stack--3" style="margin-top:32px">
        <span class="t-label t-label--ink">What we commit to</span>
        <div class="stack stack--3">
          {
            commitments.map((c, i) => (
              <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:baseline">
                <span class="t-data tx-cited">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
                <span style="font:400 16px/1.7 var(--font-display)">{c}</span>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="stack stack--3" style="margin-top:36px">
        <span class="t-label t-label--ink">Who's accountable</span>
        <div class="grid grid--2">
          <div class="c-placeholder">
            <span class="c-placeholder__flag">Placeholder</span>
            <span style="width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--paper-sunk);border:1px solid var(--line)"></span>
            <span class="t-d4" style="color:var(--ink-muted)">Founder name, role</span>
            <span class="t-sm">
              Two lines of background — what you did before and why this problem. Photo, name, and a real link.
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="c-placeholder">
            <span class="c-placeholder__flag">Placeholder</span>
            <span style="width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--paper-sunk);border:1px solid var(--line)"></span>
            <span class="t-d4" style="color:var(--ink-muted)">Method owner, role</span>
            <span class="t-sm">
              The person who signs off on attribution rules. Buyers of measurement tools ask this; answer it by
              name.
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="figcap">Fill these before launch. An anonymous measurement company is a contradiction.</span>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top:44px">
        <CtaBand
          variant="card"
          headline="The fastest way to judge us is to make us produce a number about you."
          event="about_foot"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Marketing>
